Notes: lidded stacks get a lateral-spreading credit (lid-top flux 0.85x die flux, lid mean 0.92x); the die-top and junction values are 1-D at the die centre; Si 0.6 mm = 0.050 cm2K/W (775 um: +5 K); on-die 2-3x hot spots add 5-15 K for every path except in-die (nonuniform-heatmap caveat).

### 3b. HBM (40 W/cm2) by interface over the pedestal (base-top dT under HBM max 18.7 K for H-Z2)

- paste 0.45 mm gap fill (1.16): HBM case dT 65.1 K, Tj HBM ~126 C (53 W/stack x 0.3 K/W)
- Cu pedestal + 0.1 mm PCM putty (0.28): HBM case dT 29.9 K, Tj HBM ~91 C (53 W/stack x 0.3 K/W)
- pedestal + LM 50-100 um single-field (0.04): HBM case dT 20.3 K, Tj HBM ~81 C (53 W/stack x 0.3 K/W)
- pedestal + indium (0.06): HBM case dT 21.1 K, Tj HBM ~82 C (53 W/stack x 0.3 K/W)

